{"step_index":321,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-21T07:26:56Z","model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","input_tokens":302,"cache_read_tokens":37169,"output_tokens":426,"content":"I don't have direct access to your GitHub account from here. To upload, I'll need your GitHub credentials. Here's the **easiest way** — just run these commands yourself in PowerShell:\n\n---\n\n### Option A — HTTPS (easiest, recommended)\n\nOpen **PowerShell** and run:\n\n```powershell\ncd \"C:\\Users\\abasu\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\agrisense\"\ngit remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/agrisense.git\ngit branch -M main\ngit push -u origin main\n```\n\n> Git will ask for your **GitHub username** and **password** (use a [Personal Access Token](https://github.com/settings/tokens) instead of your password — GitHub no longer accepts plain passwords).\n\n---\n\n### Option B — GitHub CLI (gh) — Fully automated\n\nIf you have [GitHub CLI](https://cli.github.com/) installed, just run:\n\n```powershell\ncd \"C:\\Users\\abasu\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\agrisense\"\ngh auth login\ngh repo create agrisense --public --source=. --remote=origin --push\n```\n\nThis creates the repo **and** pushes everything in one go. ✅\n\n---\n\n### How to get a Personal Access Token (PAT)\n\n1. Go to 👉 [github.com/settings/tokens/new](https://github.com/settings/tokens/new)\n2. Name it `agrisense-push`, check **`repo`** scope\n3. Click **Generate token** → copy it\n4. Use it as your password when Git prompts\n\n---\n\n**Tell me your GitHub username** and I'll generate the exact commands with your username pre-filled. Or if you install **GitHub CLI** (`winget install GitHub.cli`), I can run the entire push for you automatically!"}
